[2.044467, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m$ cp /tmp/claude-1000/-home-michael-alp-env-nomvula-agri-finance/7120d133-78f6-4a03-8959-fd92bf139754/scratchpad/first-note.md team-notes/2026-11-27-bicep-merged-into-main.md\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.549954, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m$ cat team-notes/README.md\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.056856, "o", "# Team Notes\r\n\r\n    **Phase: All year**\r\n\r\nMessages and notes between the pair (Lutho and Michael). Use this folder to keep the team aligned and to leave a written record of decisions.\r\n\r\n## What belongs here\r\n\r\n- **Daily alignment answers** — the three questions from [`GIT_RULES.md`](../GIT_RULES.md): which files you are changing, whether you are ready to merge, and whether the work needs a joint review.\r\n- **Meeting notes** — what was discussed, what was decided, who owns each action.\r\n- **Handover notes** — where you stopped, what is half-done, and what the other person should pick up.\r\n- **Messages to your teammate** — anything that should be in writing instead of only said aloud.\r\n\r\n## Naming\r\n\r\nOne file per note, named by date and topic so they sort in order:\r\n\r\n```\r\nYYYY-MM-DD-topic.md\r\n```\r\n\r\nFor example: `2026-11-27-bicep-merged-into-main.md`.\r\n\r\n## Rule\r\n\r\nLike everything else in this repository, notes are plain text (Markdown). No screenshots.\r\n"]
[3.05759, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m$ cp /tmp/claude-1000/-home-michael-alp-env-nomvula-agri-finance/7120d133-78f6-4a03-8959-fd92bf139754/scratchpad/README.root.md README.md\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.56683, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m$ git --no-pager diff README.md\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.072214, "o", "\u001b[1mdiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mindex e9b25d6..c19090c 100644\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1m--- a/README.md\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1m+++ b/README.md\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[36m@@ -17,10 +17,9 @@\u001b[m \u001b[mReplace the placeholders below in your first Friday (Phase 1), then commit.\u001b[m\r\n \u001b[m\r\n ## How this repository is organised\u001b[m\r\n \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[31m--Every folder has its own `README.md` explaining exactly what belongs in it. In order of the year:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m+\u001b[m\u001b[32mEvery folder has its own `README.md` explaining exactly what belongs in it. In order of the year:\u001b[m\r\n \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[31m--Rules.md is defining the global rules for anybody in the organisation who is authorised to make changes and commit to \u001b[m\r\n\u001b[31m-GITHUB.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m+\u001b[m\u001b[32m[`GIT_RULES.md`](GIT_RULES.md) defines the rules for anybody in the organisation who is authorised to make changes and commit to GitHub.\u001b[m\r\n \u001b[m\r\n - **charter/** — your project charter, business profile, and POPIA exposure assessment (Phase 1)\u001b[m\r\n - **threat-model/** — the threat model, versions 0 to 3, each kept (Phases 1 to 4)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[36m@@ -34,7 +33,9 @@\u001b[m \u001b[mGITHUB.\u001b[m\r\n - **cost/** — the costed bill of materials and scenario models (Phase 5)\u001b[m\r\n - **evidence/** — asciinema casts, scanner reports, log extracts, pipeline run records (all year)\u001b[m\r\n - **reflections/** — one reflection **per student, per phase**, in your own words (all year)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[31m--**tools**custom command line tools to ease workflow\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m+\u001b[m\u001b[32m- **tools/** — custom command-line tools that ease the workflow: `tools/recording/` (`rec`, `playrec`, `sync`, `feat`) and `tools/bicep_env/` (Bicep environment setup)\u001b[m\r\n"]
[4.072644, "o", "\u001b[32m+\u001b[m\u001b[32m- **team-notes/** — team messages and notes between Lutho and Michael: meeting notes, handovers, decisions, and who is working on which files (all year)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m+\u001b[m\r\n ## The one rule that matters most\u001b[m\r\n \u001b[m\r\n **Evidence is always text.** No screenshots, anywhere, ever. Every proof of work is a committed file, a terminal transcript (`asciinema`), a scanner report, a pipeline log, or a diagram source with its written description. This is a hard rule, it is in the rubric, and it is what makes your work fully accessible.\u001b[m\r\n"]
[4.072938, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m$ git add README.md team-notes\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.578362, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m$ git commit -m 'Add team-notes folder and update root README' -m 'Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>'\u001b[0m\r\n"]
